From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hermes <hermes@local>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 06:00:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] host: the dauth chain, as a host module

On a console the game asks the dauth system module for a token and the module does the HTTP. There
is no system module here, so this speaks the chain itself: challenge, device tokens, edge tokens,
application auth token - the four calls nx-dauth serves, in that order, over the same SecureTransport
the game's own connections use.

The domain, the device id, the port and the certificate policy are environment, not constants: no
hostname of a particular service is compiled in, and TLS_INSECURE exists only so the test can talk
to a mock with a throwaway certificate. The JWTs the servers sign are not verified here - dcert and
acert publish those keys, and the game is the party that checks them.

t_dauth_local runs the whole chain against a mock the workflow starts and asserts the token comes
back, then that the switch off refuses.

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: upstream has no network account at all; this is the client side of the dauth chain (challenge, device/edge tokens, application auth token) that any online path needs, kept behind DM_NEXTENDO
Issue: none opened yet — notes/nextendo-spike.md has the chain and the open questions

